WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.930
A mole of carbon dioxide is more
than twenty times heavier than

2
00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:05.570
a mole of hydrogen.

3
00:00:05.620 --> 00:00:09.710
Put them side by side on a balance,
and the difference is huge.

4
00:00:09.760 --> 00:00:11.630
Yet at room temperature and pressure,

5
00:00:11.680 --> 00:00:16.350
each one fills the same space:
twenty-four cubic decimetres.

6
00:00:16.400 --> 00:00:20.250
How can a heavy gas and a light
gas take up the same room?

7
00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:23.570
In this mission, you'll meet
the volume that one mole of any

8
00:00:23.620 --> 00:00:26.110
gas fills at room
temperature and pressure.

9
00:00:26.160 --> 00:00:29.810
You'll see why equal volumes
of gases hold equal numbers of

10
00:00:29.860 --> 00:00:33.110
molecules, and use that to
turn a volume into moles,

11
00:00:33.160 --> 00:00:34.790
and back again.

12
00:00:34.840 --> 00:00:38.750
Your mission: explain why a
mole of any gas fills the same

13
00:00:38.800 --> 00:00:39.850
space.
